    {
      "id": "D1",
      "statement": "Choose an error-recovery model for invalid key contracts: the implementation keeps the first duplicate member and skips a member whose key kind conflicts with earlier members.",
      "whyHuman": "The requirement asks for a working analyzer but does not define which member an invalid type's partial model should contain. The added analyzer tests check diagnostics and the absence of an analyzer exception, not which member should be retained for subsequent constructor analysis or generation. A test can describe the selected recovery policy but cannot establish that it is the intended policy.",
      "options": [
        "Report the diagnostic, keep the first duplicate, and skip mismatched-kind members, as implemented.",
        "Report the diagnostic but replace the earlier entry with the last duplicate.",
        "Report the diagnostic and abandon collection of the whole type instead of retaining a partial member set.",
        "Adopt different recovery policies for property and field paths."
      ],
      "hunkIds": [
