      "id": "F1",
      "statement": "A remaining analyzer-exception path exists for the first keyed field with a null string key, including on a suppressed type. In the field loop, intKey and stringKey can both be null; when searchFirst is true, isIntKey becomes false and execution reaches stringMembers.ContainsKey(stringKey!) with a null key. The null-forgiving operator does not prevent Dictionary's null-key exception. The property path has an explicit stringKey-is-not-null branch, but the field path does not. This path was not shown to be introduced by the patch, but it leaves another way for collection to fail before the SuppressSourceGeneration return.",
